  "problem": "Let $u=\u27e81,-3,2\u27e9$ and $v=\u27e84,2,-1\u27e9.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=\u27e8${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-3)(-1)-(2)(2))i-((1)(-1)-(2)(4))j+((1)(2)-(-3)(4))k \\\\  & =(3-4)i-(-1-8)j+(2+12)k \\\\  & =-1i+9j+14k \\\\  & =\u27e8-1,9,14\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
